    "updated_at": "2024-12-06T02:08:28Z",
    "body": "Chrome and Safari (haven't tested Firefox) violate the next line as well:\r\n\r\n> User agents should not display [non-persistent notification](https://notifications.spec.whatwg.org/#non-persistent-notification) in a platform’s \"notification center\" (if available).\r\n\r\nChrome on Windows and ChromeOS (haven't tested other platforms) add non-persistent notifications to the platform's \"notification center\". Safari does as well, though as mentioned above it removes them when the tab is navigated or closed. Chrome does not.",
